l that usually emulates the effect of the Unquiet Dead boon, but can actually raise the subject as a temporary Follower (up to 3 dots, unless you've accidentally summoned something massively more powerful as per this relic's Flaw). The raised dead is usually made Hollow by this process, and the only way to put it down again is to reverse the process (which requires spending another point of Legend); otherwise, the Follower stays under your control until the end of the current Story, at which point it is free to do as it wills. A given Fragment can only control one Follower at a time -- attempting to raise another one frees the current one from the Scion's control.</li> <li><b>Flaw</b>: Sometimes it is not possible for the Scion or sorcerer to put down what they called up. Gravestones are lost or switched, or the inscription might have been wrong. It's possible that what the Scion <i>thinks</i> they're summoning is something that they aren't prepared to face. The Storyguide may spend a point of Tension when the Fragment's Knack is used to switch out for someone (or some<i>thing</i>) dangerous and hostile. This is usually at least a Rival-level Antagonist who is <i>not</i> happy with the Scion or sorcerer and is also not in any way under their control.</li> </ul>\u200b<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T14:17:00-07:00","id":1505449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1496459-would-you-mix-scion-and-the-mythos?p=1505435#post1505435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a way to inject Cosmic Horror while describing actual Astronomy stuff in a mythic way. For instance, <a href=\"https://www.sci.news/astronomy/science-white-dwarf-made-diamond-02016.html\" target=\"_blank\">diamond stars</a> (stellar remnants that have fused much of their mass into carbon, which has crystalized) are a real thing they've discovered, and <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/dead-planets-broadcast-after-star-explodes-2019-8\" target=\"_blank\">white dwarfs can emit radio signals</a> we can detect for billions of years. Combine that with a <a href=\"https://hitchhikers.fandom.com/wiki/Total_Perspective_Vortex\" target=\"_blank\">total perspective vortex</a>-like idea of existential dread at the sheer vastness of cosmic time, and it made for a really cool idea for an entity. Lovecraft found ways of making colors, angles, music, paintings, and freaking <i>air conditioning</i> scary with good description -- it's the same sort of principle here. And it's one of the main ways you can make the Mythos work with the idea of Scion -- by focusing on the mythic elements. Lovecraft used his Mythos to explore what he was afraid of -- this is a thing that mythology has been doing forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T13:50:11-07:00","id":1505935,"title":"","content":"One take I thought of is having mythos beings be the result of gods and other similar beings that found themselves surviving being disconnected from Humanity and its collective memory that is Fate. The write up of the proto-Indo-European god that is Dyeus Pitar is a good example of the idea. Imagine the forgotten gods of the neanderthals or of the cultures that the proto-Indo-European ended up displacing, the gods of the Basque's lost cultural relatives or the gods that form when humanity just came out of Africa. And then the rediscovery of relics results in a connection forming to the lost deities once more.<br /> <br /> Could even use the whole 'Mythos beings are outside of Fate' by having Fate represent Humanity's never ending quest to find meaning in the universe and the very ability for pattern recognition. Had the Face of Mars remained more culturally relevant, it might actually develop into a genius loci spirit out of humanity's collective will power alone like the Man on the Moon and the Jade Rabbits. Though that also means cryptids, aliens, and other modern beings like Slenderman are technically recently created denizens of the World if you apply the Denizen rules for mythological beings living in society. If I understand that right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6163-yama951","name":"Yama951","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T14:06:08-07:00","id":1505938,"title":"","content":"\u201cFate is humanity's collective memory\u201d and \u201cdeveloping into a genius loci spirit out of humanity's collective willpower alone\u201d strike me as being ideas more suitable for Mage: the Ascension than Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T00:45:06-07:00","id":1506018,"title":"","content":"I am not completely opposed to mixing Mythos and Scion, but I would take a different take from the Mythos book. Basically the Mythos would be treated as Titans at best. I would consider the mutation rules on the table for them. Pretty much every pantheon has a equivalent of on Elder Sign to lock out Mythos entities (and potentially shut down the use of Awareness). I wouldn't put them outside Fate, but would rather favour tying their Fatebindings to places and objects over people.<br /> I'd even go so far as to have the Orisha and the Titanomachy oppose them as a threat.<br /> <br /> The Mythos does not play nice with others within their own continuity and by the rules as written are potentially a lot more powerful. I'd houserule that Awareness cannot be used for Divine Rule or Divine Opposition. Remember Awareness exists alongside Legend and can be used for pretty much everything Legend can unless stated otherwise.<br /> <br /> My primary issue with Mythos is its own book pretty much states that they are objectively correct and supports this mechanically; which i have issues in a setting that takes the concept of &quot;All Myths are True&quot; and runs with it. But there is enough to make it workable if you are careful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T21:57:09-07:00","id":1506210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1496459-would-you-mix-scion-and-the-mythos?p=1506018#post1506018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not completely opposed to mixing Mythos and Scion, but I would take a different take from the Mythos book. Basically the Mythos would be treated as Titans at best. I would consider the mutation rules on the table for them. Pretty much every pantheon has a equivalent of on Elder Sign to lock out Mythos entities (and potentially shut down the use of Awareness). I wouldn't put them outside Fate, but would rather favour tying their Fatebindings to places and objects over people.<br /> I'd even go so far as to have the Orisha and the Titanomachy oppose them as a threat.<br /> <br /> The Mythos does not play nice with others within their own continuity and by the rules as written are potentially a lot more powerful. I'd houserule that Awareness cannot be used for Divine Rule or Divine Opposition. Remember Awareness exists alongside Legend and can be used for pretty much everything Legend can unless stated otherwise.<br /> <br /> My primary issue with Mythos is its own book pretty much states that they are objectively correct and supports this mechanically; which i have issues in a setting that takes the concept of &quot;All Myths are True&quot; and runs with it. But there is enough to make it workable if you are careful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a similar take I would go with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T20:53:41-07:00","id":1507365,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a group of Scions who learn of the Mythos and decide to Band together to protect The World from the Outsiders. But to do so they have to kind of flirt with the knowledge of the Mythos and may be tempted by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T21:19:44-07:00","id":1507369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1496459-would-you-mix-scion-and-the-mythos?p=1507365#post1507365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of a group of Scions who learn of the Mythos and decide to Band together to protect The World from the Outsiders. But to do so they have to kind of flirt with the knowledge of the Mythos and may be tempted by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dun dun duuun...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}